<title>USA: Toyota Camry rated &quot;best&quot; in crash tests.</title>
<headline>Toyota Camry rated &quot;best&quot; in crash tests.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toyota Motor Corp's Camry model was rated a &quot;best pick&quot; on the basis of crash tests conducted by the Insurance Institute for Highway Safety, the industry-backed group said on Monday.</p>
<p>In other tests of midsize four-door cars, the institute rated General Motors Corp's Pontiac Grand Prix &quot;acceptable&quot; and the Hyundai Motor Co Ltd's Sonata as &quot;poor.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Best picks&quot; among midsize four-door cars announced earlier were Ford Motor Co's Taurus/Mercury Sable, GM's Chevrolet Lumina and the Volvo 850.</p>
</text>
